IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rcrd-rebates`

-- Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) -- the Q&A layer: the questions people ask, with the seat
-- and the situation as parameters, so that one deployment serves every seat and the question form drops the questions
-- that do not arise.
--
-- SEATS (`my role`, the first input of every exported question, "Which of these describes you"):
--   * the pensioner or senior who owns or lives in the home -- the baseline's seat, whose 27 questions are asked here by
--     calling the baseline's functions in rcrd-rebates.l4;
--   * the spouse or de facto partner of a registered pensioner or senior -- for whom deferred charges stay deferred after
--     the pensioner's death or move (s 45, "notwithstanding that the spouse or de facto partner may not be an eligible
--     person"), and who may be treated as registered after the death (s 32A);
--   * a person buying, inheriting, lending on or administering a home on which rates or charges were deferred -- for
--     whom the deferred charges are a charge on the land (ss 46, 48, 49) that falls due on death, sale or a move (s 44(2)).
-- A question about another role answers `does not arise for you` without reading any other input. The administrative
-- authority (the local government, the Water Corporation), the Minister, the Registrar of Titles and the CEO who issues
-- State concession cards are never seats: what they may or must do appears as what it means for the person asking.
--
-- SITUATIONS (design D8 of the graffiti encoding): within a role, a question that arises only in a situation takes that
-- situation's fact straight after `my role`, and when it does not hold answers `does not arise for you` without reading
-- anything else. The questions of one situation share one input, character for character. They are:
--   * for the pensioner or senior: `I have deferred rates or charges on my home` (ss 35(4), 44(2), 45, 46, 49);
--   * for the partner: `what has happened to my spouse or de facto partner` (an enumeration): `my partner has died` opens
--     the four questions of ss 32A and 45(1); `my partner has stopped living in our home` opens the one of s 45(2); the
--     other values give `does not arise for you`. The form asks it once for all five;
--   * the buyer or executor has none: the role is itself the situation (a home with deferred charges).
-- A question that arises in every situation of its role (eligibility, registration, the rebate and its limits, the day
-- to pay, deferment) takes no situation input. The helpers that read the partner's situation list every value, with no
-- OTHERWISE (graffiti finding 31).
--
-- No exported question takes a DEONTIC or EVENT input. The baseline's records (`My cards and circumstances`, `My home`,
-- `My deferment circumstances`) are taken as the baseline takes them. Days are YYYYMMDD numbers, as in the baseline.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md, "Q&A layer (seat and situations as parameters)".

§ `Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) -- the questions people ask`

§§ `Who is asking, and the shape of the answers`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home`
    `My spouse or de facto partner is, or was, the pensioner or senior registered for our home`
    `I am buying, inheriting, lending on or administering a home on which rates or charges were deferred`

DECLARE `Yes or no` IS ONE OF
    yes
    no
    `does not arise for you`

DECLARE `Amount` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER

-- The rebate questions' answer: s 40(5)-(7) divide by the days in the charged period (CY), so a period of no days has
-- no rebate to work out, and says so rather than dividing by zero.
DECLARE `Rebate answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    amount HAS dollars IS A NUMBER
    `the charged period must have at least one day`

DECLARE `Share` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `share of the charge` HAS `fraction` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Limit` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `limit of` HAS dollars IS A NUMBER
    `no limit`

DECLARE `Day answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `by` HAS `the day, as YYYYMMDD` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Days` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `days after the notice` HAS `days` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Years` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `within` HAS `years` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `Basis answer` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `register` HAS `basis` IS A `My basis of eligibility`

DECLARE `Outcome` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `outcome` HAS `what follows` IS A `What paying or not paying leads to`

DECLARE `How the deferred charges rank` IS ONE OF
    `ahead of it`
    `equally with it`
    `behind it`

DECLARE `Ranking` IS ONE OF
    `does not arise for you`
    `ranks` HAS `how` IS A `How the deferred charges rank`

-- The partner's situation (D8).
DECLARE `What has happened to my partner` IS ONE OF
    `my partner has died`
    `my partner has stopped living in our home`
    `neither of these`

-- s 46: the claims the deferred charges are ranked against.
DECLARE `Other claim on the land` IS ONE OF
    `a mortgage or other charge not created by an Act`
    `another charge created by an Act`
    `an amount owed to the Housing Authority under the housing Acts or a housing scheme`
    `an amount owed to the Defence Homes Corporation`

-- s 44(2), from the side of the person dealing with the land.
DECLARE `What happened to the pensioner or the home` IS ONE OF
    `the pensioner died`
    `the home stopped being the pensioner's, for example it was sold`
    `the pensioner stopped living there`

§§ `Carrying the baseline's answers, and the helpers the new seats need`

GIVEN `it holds` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`yes if` `it holds` MEANS
    IF `it holds` THEN yes ELSE no

-- The baseline answers -1 where the Regulations prescribe no limit.
GIVEN `the number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Limit`
`as a limit` `the number` MEANS
    IF `the number` LESS THAN 0 THEN `no limit` ELSE `limit of` `the number`

-- The partner's two situations. Every value is listed, with no OTHERWISE.
GIVEN `what` IS A `What has happened to my partner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my partner has died, as I say` IF
    CONSIDER `what`
    WHEN `my partner has died` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `my partner has stopped living in our home` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `neither of these` THEN FALSE

GIVEN `what` IS A `What has happened to my partner`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `my partner has moved out, as I say` IF
    CONSIDER `what`
    WHEN `my partner has died` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `my partner has stopped living in our home` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `neither of these` THEN FALSE

-- s 44(2)(a) with s 45(1): on the death, the charges become payable unless the home goes on being the surviving
-- partner's ordinary place of residence; they are then further deferred until the partner dies or "ceases to be a
-- person to whom the land, for the purposes of this Act, belongs" (s 45(1)(d)). The baseline's `I die` branch carries
-- the first part.
GIVEN `I live on there` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it has stopped being mine` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`payable after my partner's death` `I live on there` `it has stopped being mine` MEANS
        `Do my deferred charges become payable` `I die` `I live on there` FALSE FALSE
    OR  `it has stopped being mine`

-- s 44(2)(c) with s 45(2): when the pensioner stops living there, the charges become payable unless they left through
-- ill-health or frailty (s 44(2)(c)(ii)) or their partner stays on (s 44(2)(c)(iii), s 45(2)); a family court order
-- providing for payment ends the s 45(2) deferral (s 45(2)(e)) but not the s 44(2)(c)(ii) one. A dependant staying on
-- (s 44(2)(c)(i)) is not asked of the partner, and is FALSE.
GIVEN `I live on there` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they left through ill-health` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a court order provides for payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`payable after my partner moved out` `I live on there` `they left through ill-health` `a court order provides for payment` MEANS
        `Do my deferred charges become payable` `I stop living there` `I live on there` `they left through ill-health` FALSE
    OR  (`a court order provides for payment` AND (NOT `they left through ill-health`))

-- s 32A(2): (a) the deceased partner's registered entitlement; (b) the land now the survivor's, or occupied under
-- s 29(1)(b)(ii); (c), (d) liable and eligible at the start of period 1 (and of period 2 if (ii) applies); (e)
-- registered before the end of period 1, or of period 2.
GIVEN `a` IS A BOOLEAN
      `b` IS A BOOLEAN
      `c` IS A BOOLEAN
      `d` IS A BOOLEAN
      `e` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`treated as registered from the next charged period` `a` `b` `c` `d` `e` MEANS
    `a` AND `b` AND `c` AND (`d` OR `e`)

-- s 32A(4A), (4B): for Water Corporation charges, registered within 2 years of the death.
GIVEN `a` IS A BOOLEAN
      `b` IS A BOOLEAN
      `c` IS A BOOLEAN
      `d` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`back-dated to my first water payment` `a` `b` `c` `d` MEANS
    `a` AND `b` AND `c` AND `d`

-- s 32A(5): "by the date specified in the notice requiring payment ... or at the end of the charged period to which the
-- notice relates, whichever is the later". Days are YYYYMMDD numbers, so the later is the larger.
GIVEN `x` IS A NUMBER
      `y` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the later of` `x` `y` MEANS
    IF `x` AT LEAST `y` THEN `x` ELSE `y`

-- s 46(1): the deferred charges are "a charge on the land ranking equally with any other charge on that land created by
-- an Act, and before any other kind of charge on that land, subject to subsections (2) and (3)"; s 46(2) gives the
-- Housing Authority priority, s 46(3) the Defence Homes Corporation. Every value is listed.
GIVEN `the claim` IS AN `Other claim on the land`
GIVETH A `How the deferred charges rank`
`how the deferred charges rank against` `the claim` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the claim`
    WHEN `a mortgage or other charge not created by an Act` THEN `ahead of it`
    WHEN `another charge created by an Act` THEN `equally with it`
    WHEN `an amount owed to the Housing Authority under the housing Acts or a housing scheme` THEN `behind it`
    WHEN `an amount owed to the Defence Homes Corporation` THEN `behind it`

-- The buyer's or executor's account of s 44(2), as the baseline's `What happens to me`.
GIVEN `what` IS A `What happened to the pensioner or the home`
GIVETH A `What happens to me`
`what happened, as the pensioner puts it` `what` MEANS
    CONSIDER `what`
    WHEN `the pensioner died` THEN `I die`
    WHEN `the home stopped being the pensioner's, for example it was sold` THEN `the home stops being mine, for example I sell it`
    WHEN `the pensioner stopped living there` THEN `I stop living there`

§§ `For the pensioner or senior ratepayer (the baseline's seat)`

-- Each question calls the baseline's function of the same subject (rcrd-rebates.l4) and restates no rule: for this
-- role, and where its situation holds, its answer is the baseline's, carried in the answer types above.

§§§ `ss 22-25 -- am I an eligible pensioner or an eligible senior`

@export Am I an eligible pensioner under any limb other than section 23(5) (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) ss 23(1)-(4), 24)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `My cards and circumstances` @desc Your concession cards, pension and means-test position
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I an eligible pensioner in my own right, under the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `yes if` (`Am I an eligible pensioner in my own right` `me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I an eligible pensioner (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) ss 3(1), 23, 24)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `My cards and circumstances` @desc Your concession cards, pension and means-test position
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I an eligible pensioner under the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `yes if` (`Am I an eligible pensioner` `me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I an eligible senior (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) ss 3(1), 22)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `My cards and circumstances` @desc Your concession cards, pension and means-test position
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I an eligible senior under the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `yes if` (`Am I an eligible senior` `me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export On which basis should I register: as an eligible pensioner or as an eligible senior (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) ss 28(3), 32(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `My cards and circumstances` @desc Your concession cards, pension and means-test position
GIVETH A `Basis answer`
`On which basis should I register, as a pensioner or as a senior` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `register` (`On which basis should I register` `me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 27, 29-29C, 30, 32 -- does my home count, and must my entitlement be registered`

@export Is my home treated as belonging to me (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) ss 27(1), 29-29C)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the home` IS A `My home` @desc Your home: your interest in it, whether you live there, and your share
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my home treated as belonging to me` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `yes if` (`Does my home belong to me` `the home`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Is my home still my ordinary place of residence, even while I am away from it (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) s 30(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the home` IS A `My home` @desc Your home: your interest in it, whether you live there, and your share
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my home still my ordinary place of residence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `yes if` (`Is my home my ordinary place of residence` `the home`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Must my entitlement to this home be registered (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) ss 23(5), 27(2), 32(3)-(4a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `My cards and circumstances` @desc Your concession cards, pension and means-test position
      `the home` IS A `My home` @desc Your home: your interest in it, whether you live there, and your share
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Must my entitlement to my home be registered` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `yes if` (`Must my entitlement be registered` `me` `the home`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Does my application to the council for a rates rebate also count for the emergency services levy (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) s 32(1a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my rates application also count for the emergency services levy` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `yes if` (`Does my rates application also cover the emergency services levy`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 33 -- arrears, and a change during the year`

@export With arrears outstanding, may I still pay only the rebated amount, or defer (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) s 33(3), (6), (7))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my basis` IS A `My basis of eligibility` @desc The basis on which you are registered
      `I owe arrears of this charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether arrears of this kind of charge are due from you
      `I have agreed an arrears arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the council or Water Corporation agreed an arrangement to pay the arrears
      `I have been given notice for breaking the arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you missed the arrangement's payments and were given written notice to pay the full charge
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`With arrears outstanding, may I still pay only the rebated amount` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `yes if` (`May I pay only the rebated amount despite arrears` `my basis` `I owe arrears of this charge` `I have agreed an arrears arrangement` `I have been given notice for breaking the arrangement`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Am I entitled to a rebate or deferment of the rates on my home under this Act (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) ss 27(2), 33(3), 40(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `My cards and circumstances` @desc Your concession cards, pension and means-test position
      `the home` IS A `My home` @desc Your home: your interest in it, whether you live there, and your share
      `I owe arrears of this charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether arrears of this kind of charge are due from you
      `I have agreed an arrears arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and the council or Water Corporation agreed an arrangement to pay the arrears
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I entitled to a rebate or deferment of the rates on my home` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `yes if` (`Am I entitled to a rebate or deferment` `me` `the home` `I owe arrears of this charge` `I have agreed an arrears arrangement`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If I die, stop being eligible, or the home stops being mine, does my rebate still apply for that charged period (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) s 33(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `it is a Water Corporation charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the charge is made by the Water Corporation
      `the charged period is the one in which the change happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you ask about the charged period in which the change happened, rather than a later one
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Does my rebate still apply for the charged period of a change` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `yes if` (`Does my rebate still apply for the charged period of the change` `it is a Water Corporation charge` `the charged period is the one in which the change happened`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `s 40 and the Regulations -- how much is my rebate`

@export What share of the charge is my rebate before any limit (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) s 40(9))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my basis` IS A `My basis of eligibility` @desc The basis on which you are registered
GIVETH A `Share`
`What share of the charge is my rebate, before any limit` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `share of the charge` (`What fraction of the charge is my rebate` `my basis`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What is the most rebate the Regulations allow me on this kind of charge (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Regulations 1992 (WA) rr 3(2), 4(1A), 4(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my basis` IS A `My basis of eligibility` @desc The basis on which you are registered
      `the kind` IS A `Kind of charge` @desc The kind of prescribed charge
GIVETH A `Limit`
`What is the most rebate the Regulations allow me on this kind of charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `as a limit` (`What is the prescribed limit on my rebate` `my basis` `the kind`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What part of the charge is mine, after apportionment for shared ownership and other uses (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) ss 28(1)(b), 28(2), 40(1A))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the home` IS A `My home` @desc Your home: your interest in it, whether you live there, and your share
      `the charge` IS A NUMBER @desc The whole prescribed charge on the land for the charged period, in dollars
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What part of the charge is mine, after apportionment` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `amount` (`What part of the charge is mine` `the home` `the charge`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much is my rebate on this charge for the charged period (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) ss 28, 40(4)-(7), (9); Regulations rr 3, 4)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the kind` IS A `Kind of charge` @desc The kind of prescribed charge
      `the home` IS A `My home` @desc Your home: your interest in it, whether you live there, and your share
      `the charge` IS A NUMBER @desc The whole prescribed charge on the land for the charged period, in dollars
      `days registered as a pensioner` IS A NUMBER @desc Days of the charged period you were registered as an eligible pensioner
      `days registered as a senior` IS A NUMBER @desc Days of the charged period you were registered as an eligible senior
      `days in the charged period` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days in the charged period
GIVETH A `Rebate answer`
`How much is my rebate on this charge` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN
        IF `days in the charged period` AT MOST 0
        THEN `the charged period must have at least one day`
        ELSE `amount` (`How much is my rebate` `the kind` `the home` `the charge` `days registered as a pensioner` `days registered as a senior` `days in the charged period`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How much must I pay after my rebate: the rebated amount (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) ss 3(1), 40(1A), 40(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the kind` IS A `Kind of charge` @desc The kind of prescribed charge
      `the home` IS A `My home` @desc Your home: your interest in it, whether you live there, and your share
      `the charge` IS A NUMBER @desc The whole prescribed charge on the land for the charged period, in dollars
      `days registered as a pensioner` IS A NUMBER @desc Days of the charged period you were registered as an eligible pensioner
      `days registered as a senior` IS A NUMBER @desc Days of the charged period you were registered as an eligible senior
      `days in the charged period` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days in the charged period
GIVETH A `Rebate answer`
`How much must I pay after my rebate` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN
        IF `days in the charged period` AT MOST 0
        THEN `the charged period must have at least one day`
        ELSE `amount` (`What is my rebated amount` `the kind` `the home` `the charge` `days registered as a pensioner` `days registered as a senior` `days in the charged period`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export As a senior, do I get a rebate on the underground electricity service charge this year (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) s 40(2A))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my basis` IS A `My basis of eligibility` @desc The basis on which you are registered
      `this is the first year of the charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this is the first year, or part year, for which the underground electricity charge is made
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`As a senior, do I get a rebate on the underground electricity charge this year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `yes if` (`Do I get a rebate on the underground electricity charge` `my basis` `this is the first year of the charge`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 40(2), (3A), 41, 44(1) -- by when must I pay the rebated amount`

@export By what day must I pay the rebated amount of my council rates or emergency services levy (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) s 40(2)(b), (3A))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the rating year` IS A NUMBER @desc The rating year, named by the year in which it ends (2073/74 is 2074)
      `the Minister allowed me an extended period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Minister, satisfied of exceptional circumstances, allowed you an extended period
      `the end of the extended period` IS A NUMBER @desc The last day of that extended period, as YYYYMMDD (ignored if none)
GIVETH A `Day answer`
`By what day must I pay the rebated amount of my rates or levy` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `by` (`By what day must I pay my rebated rates` `the rating year` `the Minister allowed me an extended period` `the end of the extended period`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How many days after my Water Corporation notice is my final payment day for the rebated amount (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) s 3(1), s 40(2)(a))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `extra days the Water Corporation allowed me` IS A NUMBER @desc Further days beyond the 50th day that the Water Corporation determined for you (0 if none)
GIVETH A `Days`
`As a pensioner or senior, how many days after my water notice is my final payment day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `days after the notice` (`How many days after my water notice is my final payment day` `extra days the Water Corporation allowed me`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export What happens if I pay, or do not pay, the rebated amount by the day (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) ss 40(2), 41, 44(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `my basis` IS A `My basis of eligibility` @desc The basis on which you are registered
      `I paid the rebated amount in time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you paid the whole rebated amount by the day
      `I may defer this charge` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether deferment is open to you under section 43 (see that question)
GIVETH AN `Outcome`
`What happens if I pay, or do not pay, the rebated amount by the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `outcome` (`What happens to the charge` `my basis` `I paid the rebated amount in time` `I may defer this charge`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 43, 47 -- may I defer paying`

@export May I defer paying my rates and charges (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) ss 43, 47)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `me` IS A `My cards and circumstances` @desc Your concession cards, pension and means-test position
      `the home` IS A `My home` @desc Your home: your interest in it, whether you live there, and your share
      `the circumstances` IS A `My deferment circumstances` @desc Co-ownership and the authority's view of recoverability
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I defer paying my rates and charges` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `yes if` (`May I defer payment` `me` `the home` `the circumstances`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 35(4), 44(2), 45, 46, 49 -- my deferred charges`

@export Do my deferred rates and charges become payable now (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) ss 44(2), 45)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have deferred rates or charges on my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether payment of any rates or charges on your home has been deferred under the Act and remains unpaid (the questions on deferred charges, ss 35(4), 44(2), 45, 46 and 49, arise only then)
      `the event` IS A `What happens to me` @desc What has happened
      `my spouse or de facto partner goes on living there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your spouse or de facto partner continues to live there as their ordinary place of residence
      `I left because of ill-health, frailty or another cause beyond my control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you left for a reason outside your control
      `an eligible dependant who pays the charge stays on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a dependant within section 31(1) stays on, paying the charge
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Do my deferred rates and charges become payable now` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN
        IF `I have deferred rates or charges on my home`
        THEN `yes if` (`Do my deferred charges become payable` `the event` `my spouse or de facto partner goes on living there` `I left because of ill-health, frailty or another cause beyond my control` `an eligible dependant who pays the charge stays on`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Are my unpaid deferred charges a charge on my home (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) s 46(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have deferred rates or charges on my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether payment of any rates or charges on your home has been deferred under the Act and remains unpaid (the questions on deferred charges, ss 35(4), 44(2), 45, 46 and 49, arise only then)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Are my unpaid deferred charges a charge on my home` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN
        IF `I have deferred rates or charges on my home`
        THEN `yes if` (`Are my deferred charges a charge on my home`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the passage of time (the Limitation Act 2005) stop my deferred charges being recovered (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) s 49)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have deferred rates or charges on my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether payment of any rates or charges on your home has been deferred under the Act and remains unpaid (the questions on deferred charges, ss 35(4), 44(2), 45, 46 and 49, arise only then)
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the passage of time stop my deferred charges being recovered` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN
        IF `I have deferred rates or charges on my home`
        THEN `yes if` (`Can time bar recovery of my deferred charges`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If I stop being eligible only because my income or assets rose above the means test, may I keep the deferment I already have (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) s 35(4))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `I have deferred rates or charges on my home` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether payment of any rates or charges on your home has been deferred under the Act and remains unpaid (the questions on deferred charges, ss 35(4), 44(2), 45, 46 and 49, arise only then)
      `the only reason is that my income or assets rose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a rise in income or assets above the means test is the only reason you stopped being eligible
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`May I keep the deferment I already have if my income or assets rose` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN
        IF `I have deferred rates or charges on my home`
        THEN `yes if` (`May I keep my existing deferment` `the only reason is that my income or assets rose`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 35, 38 -- changes I must report, and the penalty`

@export What is the most I can be fined for failing to report a change, or for a false claim (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) s 38(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH AN `Amount`
`What is the most I can be fined for failing to report a change` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `amount` (`What is the most I can be fined`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Within how many years after the offence must a prosecution be started (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) s 38(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Years`
`Within how many years after the offence must a prosecution be started` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am a pensioner or senior, and I own or live in my home` THEN `within` (`Within how many years must I be prosecuted`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For the spouse or de facto partner of a registered pensioner or senior (ss 32A, 44(2), 45)`

-- s 45 keeps deferred charges deferred in favour of a spouse or de facto partner "notwithstanding that the spouse or
-- de facto partner may not be an eligible person"; s 32A lets a surviving partner be treated as registered from the
-- charged period after the death. Every question here arises only in one of the two situations of
-- `what has happened to my spouse or de facto partner`.

§§§ `ss 32A, 44(2), 45 -- after my partner's death`

@export If charges on our home were deferred, do they become payable now that my spouse or de facto partner has died (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) ss 44(2)(a), 45(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what has happened to my spouse or de facto partner` IS A `What has happened to my partner` @desc Whether your spouse or de facto partner, who was registered for the home, has died, or has stopped living in the home while you live on there (if neither, these questions do not arise)
      `the home is still my ordinary place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you go on living in the home as your ordinary place of residence
      `the home has stopped being mine, for example I sold it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, since the death, you have ceased to be a person to whom the home belongs under the Act, for example because you sold it or gave up your interest (s 45(1)(d))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Now that my partner has died, do the deferred charges on our home become payable` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `My spouse or de facto partner is, or was, the pensioner or senior registered for our home` THEN
        IF `my partner has died, as I say` `what has happened to my spouse or de facto partner`
        THEN `yes if` (`payable after my partner's death` `the home is still my ordinary place of residence` `the home has stopped being mine, for example I sold it`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export For council rates and other charges that are not Water Corporation charges, am I treated as registered from the start of the charged period after my partner's death (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) s 32A(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what has happened to my spouse or de facto partner` IS A `What has happened to my partner` @desc Whether your spouse or de facto partner, who was registered for the home, has died, or has stopped living in the home while you live on there (if neither, these questions do not arise)
      `my partner had a registered entitlement for the home immediately before they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your partner was registered under the Act for a rebate or deferment on the home immediately before their death
      `since the death the home belongs to me, or I occupy it, as section 32A allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, since the death, the home belongs to you as a former joint tenant or tenant in common with your partner, or as a beneficiary under their will or intestacy, or you occupy it during the distribution of their estate as a prospective owner, life tenant or person entitled under the will to live there (s 32A(2)(b), (4A)(b))
      `I was liable for the charge, and eligible, at the start of the next charged period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the start of the charged period after the one in which the charge was last payable by your partner, you were liable to pay the charge and eligible to apply for registration
      `I was registered before the end of that period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your entitlement was registered, on your application, before the end of that next charged period
      `I was also liable and eligible at the start of the period after that, and was registered before its end` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were also liable and eligible at the start of the second charged period after it, and your entitlement was registered before the end of that second period
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Am I treated as registered from the charged period after my partner's death` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `My spouse or de facto partner is, or was, the pensioner or senior registered for our home` THEN
        IF `my partner has died, as I say` `what has happened to my spouse or de facto partner`
        THEN `yes if` (`treated as registered from the next charged period` `my partner had a registered entitlement for the home immediately before they died` `since the death the home belongs to me, or I occupy it, as section 32A allows` `I was liable for the charge, and eligible, at the start of the next charged period` `I was registered before the end of that period` `I was also liable and eligible at the start of the period after that, and was registered before its end`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export If I am treated as registered under section 32A(2) or (3), by what day may I pay the rebated amount (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) s 32A(5))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what has happened to my spouse or de facto partner` IS A `What has happened to my partner` @desc Whether your spouse or de facto partner, who was registered for the home, has died, or has stopped living in the home while you live on there (if neither, these questions do not arise)
      `the day the notice requires payment, as YYYYMMDD` IS A NUMBER @desc The date specified in the notice requiring payment of the charge, as YYYYMMDD
      `the last day of the charged period, as YYYYMMDD` IS A NUMBER @desc The last day of the charged period the notice relates to, as YYYYMMDD (30 June for council rates)
GIVETH A `Day answer`
`By what day may I pay the rebated amount as a surviving partner treated as registered` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `My spouse or de facto partner is, or was, the pensioner or senior registered for our home` THEN
        IF `my partner has died, as I say` `what has happened to my spouse or de facto partner`
        THEN `by` (`the later of` `the day the notice requires payment, as YYYYMMDD` `the last day of the charged period, as YYYYMMDD`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export For Water Corporation charges, am I treated as registered from the day I first became liable after my partner's death (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) s 32A(4A), (4B))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what has happened to my spouse or de facto partner` IS A `What has happened to my partner` @desc Whether your spouse or de facto partner, who was registered for the home, has died, or has stopped living in the home while you live on there (if neither, these questions do not arise)
      `my partner had a registered entitlement for the home immediately before they died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your partner was registered under the Act for a rebate or deferment on the home immediately before their death
      `since the death the home belongs to me, or I occupy it, as section 32A allows` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, since the death, the home belongs to you as a former joint tenant or tenant in common with your partner, or as a beneficiary under their will or intestacy, or you occupy it during the distribution of their estate as a prospective owner, life tenant or person entitled under the will to live there (s 32A(2)(b), (4A)(b))
      `I was eligible when I first became liable for a Water Corporation charge on the home after the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when you first became liable to pay a Water Corporation charge on the home after the death, you were eligible to apply for registration
      `I was registered within 2 years of the death` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your entitlement was registered by the Water Corporation, on your application, within 2 years of your partner's death
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Is my Water Corporation registration back-dated after my partner's death` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `My spouse or de facto partner is, or was, the pensioner or senior registered for our home` THEN
        IF `my partner has died, as I say` `what has happened to my spouse or de facto partner`
        THEN `yes if` (`back-dated to my first water payment` `my partner had a registered entitlement for the home immediately before they died` `since the death the home belongs to me, or I occupy it, as section 32A allows` `I was eligible when I first became liable for a Water Corporation charge on the home after the death` `I was registered within 2 years of the death`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§§ `ss 44(2)(c), 45(2) -- after my partner moved out`

@export If charges on our home were deferred, do they become payable now that my spouse or de facto partner has stopped living there (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) ss 44(2)(c), 45(2))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what has happened to my spouse or de facto partner` IS A `What has happened to my partner` @desc Whether your spouse or de facto partner, who was registered for the home, has died, or has stopped living in the home while you live on there (if neither, these questions do not arise)
      `the home is still my ordinary place of residence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you go on living in the home as your ordinary place of residence
      `my partner left because of ill-health, frailty or another cause beyond their control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your partner stopped living in the home because of ill-health, frailty or another cause outside their control, for example to go into care (s 44(2)(c)(ii))
      `a court order in a family matter provides for payment of the charges` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an order of a court in a family matter provides for the deferred charges to be paid (s 45(2)(e))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Now that my partner has moved out, do the deferred charges on our home become payable` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `My spouse or de facto partner is, or was, the pensioner or senior registered for our home` THEN
        IF `my partner has moved out, as I say` `what has happened to my spouse or de facto partner`
        THEN `yes if` (`payable after my partner moved out` `the home is still my ordinary place of residence` `my partner left because of ill-health, frailty or another cause beyond their control` `a court order in a family matter provides for payment of the charges`)
        ELSE `does not arise for you`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

§§ `For a person buying, inheriting, lending on or administering a home with deferred charges (ss 44(2), 45, 46, 48, 49)`

-- The role is a person dealing with land on which deferred charges remain unpaid: the executor, the beneficiary, the
-- buyer, the lender. Every question here arises for every such person, so none takes a situation input (D8).

§§§ `ss 44(2), 45, 46, 48, 49 -- the deferred charges on this land`

@export Are the unpaid deferred rates and charges a charge on this land (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) s 46(1))?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Are the unpaid deferred charges a charge on this land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying, inheriting, lending on or administering a home on which rates or charges were deferred` THEN `yes if` `Are my deferred charges a charge on my home`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export How do the deferred charges rank against this other claim on the land (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) s 46)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `the other claim` IS AN `Other claim on the land` @desc The other claim on the land you are comparing with the deferred charges: a mortgage or other charge not created by an Act; another charge created by an Act; an amount owed to the Housing Authority under the State Housing Act 1946, the Housing Act 1980 or a housing scheme; or an amount owed to the Defence Homes Corporation
GIVETH A `Ranking`
`How do the deferred charges rank against this other claim on the land` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying, inheriting, lending on or administering a home on which rates or charges were deferred` THEN `ranks` (`how the deferred charges rank against` `the other claim`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Have the deferred charges become payable, so that the council or Water Corporation may recover them (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) ss 44(2), 45)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
      `what happened` IS A `What happened to the pensioner or the home` @desc What has happened: the pensioner died; the home stopped being theirs, for example it was sold; or they stopped living there
      `the pensioner's spouse or de facto partner goes on living there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the pensioner's spouse or de facto partner continues to live in the home as their ordinary place of residence (ss 44(2)(c)(iii), 45)
      `the pensioner left because of ill-health, frailty or another cause beyond their control` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the pensioner stopped living there because of ill-health, frailty or another cause outside their control, for example to go into care
      `a dependant of the pensioner who pays the charge stays on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a dependant of the pensioner who lived there with them stays on, eligible and paying the charge (s 31(1))
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Have the deferred charges become payable, so that they may be recovered` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying, inheriting, lending on or administering a home on which rates or charges were deferred` THEN `yes if` (`Do my deferred charges become payable` (`what happened, as the pensioner puts it` `what happened`) `the pensioner's spouse or de facto partner goes on living there` `the pensioner left because of ill-health, frailty or another cause beyond their control` `a dependant of the pensioner who pays the charge stays on`)
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the passage of time (the Limitation Act 2005) stop the deferred charges being recovered from this land (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) s 49)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the passage of time stop the deferred charges being recovered` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying, inheriting, lending on or administering a home on which rates or charges were deferred` THEN `yes if` `Can time bar recovery of my deferred charges`
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`

@export Can the charge for the deferred charges be recorded on the land's title by the Registrar of Titles (Rates and Charges (Rebates and Deferments) Act 1992 (WA) s 48)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A Role @desc Which of these describes you
GIVETH A `Yes or no`
`Can the charge for the deferred charges be recorded on the title` MEANS
    CONSIDER `my role`
    WHEN `I am buying, inheriting, lending on or administering a home on which rates or charges were deferred` THEN yes
    OTHERWISE `does not arise for you`
